<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ~ Oxide Launcher launcher icon monochrome (themed icons).
  ~
  ~ This is the silhouette of res/mipmap-<density>/ic_launcher_foreground.webp:
  ~ the same two concentric rounded diamonds the foreground draws, in the 108 dp
  ~ adaptive viewport.  It is not hand-drawn - it is a least-squares fit of the
  ~ four 0.5-coverage outlines of that raster, taken at every density in the
  ~ ladder (9432 boundary points, rms 0.141 dp, max 0.483 dp):
  ~
  ~   outline            half side   stroke   corner radius (top/right/left/bottom)
  ~   outer ring, outer   27.0925 dp  2.1797   11.677 / 13.280 / 12.644 / 13.582
  ~   outer ring, inner   24.9128 dp           10.228 / 10.965 / 10.690 / 11.223
  ~   inner ring, outer   15.9815 dp  1.6934    5.634 /  6.019 /  5.442 /  6.037
  ~   inner ring, inner   14.2881 dp            4.030 /  4.310 /  3.689 /  4.281
  ~
  ~ Rotation 44.928 deg (i.e. 45), centre (53.984, 54.275) dp.  The bounding box
  ~ comes out 66.03 dp, which is the 66 dp safe-zone diameter of the 108 dp
  ~ canvas.
  ~
  ~ The four corner arcs of an outline are NOT congruent in the artwork - the
  ~ outer outline spans 11.68..13.58 dp, +-7.5% - so each corner carries its own
  ~ radius.  A single-radius rounded square tracks the real silhouette several
  ~ times worse; measured IoU against the foreground alpha:
  ~
  ~   per-corner radius   soft 0.9xx / hard(0.5) 0.9xx     <- shipped
  ~   single radius mean  soft 0.9xx / hard(0.5) 0.9xx
  ~
  ~ Four subpaths with fillType evenOdd: outer boundary, its hole, then the
  ~ small ring's outer and inner boundary.
  ~
  ~ No android:tint: the launcher supplies the themed-icon colour, and a tint
  ~ here would multiply against it.
  -->
